  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "On the Jan 5 '10 committer call, Asger pointed out that Kare mentioned this when talking about consistent naming...the info:fedora URIs would ideally be info:fcrepo.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We need to consider the impact of doing this and decide if the consistency is worth the cost.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "[ Impact ]",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "1) Need to register a new info: prefix with the NISO info URI registry",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "2) Need to decide how to deprecate \"info:fedora\"...just drop it, or support both for some period of time?",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "3) Existing RDF queries would need to change",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
